A Robot Linear Rail is a precision mechanical motion system, also known as a robot linear track or seventh axis, consisting of a guide rail and a moving carriage that enables robots or automated equipment to travel along a predefined linear path with high accuracy, repeatability and load capacity. By extending the working range and flexibility of robotic systems, linear rails are essential to modern industrial automation and material‑handling applications.
